# do daily/weekly/monthly maintenance
# min	hour	day	month	weekday	command
# */15	*	*	*	*	run-parts /etc/periodic/15min
# 0	*	*	*	*	run-parts /etc/periodic/hourly
# 0	2	*	*	*	run-parts /etc/periodic/daily
# 0	3	*	*	6	run-parts /etc/periodic/weekly
# 0	5	1	*	*	run-parts /etc/periodic/monthly

# These cron jobs have been moved to the Rust application (main.rs):
# - PUT /session: Now handled by spawn_sync_cron_job() - runs every 5 minutes
# - PUT /status_history: Now handled by spawn_status_history_cron_job() - runs daily at midnight
# Commented out to prevent duplicate execution:
# *	*	*	*	*	curl -X PUT back:8000/session
# 0	0	*	*	*	curl -X PUT back:8000/status_history
